fault": false, "description": "", "archived_at": null, "archived_by": null}, {"id": 7494789387, "node_id": "LA_kwDOAgUK288AAAABvrlpCw", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/labels/provider:standard", "name": "provider:standard", "color": "bfd4f2", "default": false, "description": "", "archived_at": null, "archived_by": null}, {"id": 7619732633, "node_id": "LA_kwDOAgUK288AAAABxivkmQ", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/labels/provider:edge", "name": "provider:edge", "color": "bfd4f2", "default": false, "description": "Edge Executor / Worker (AIP-69) / edge3", "archived_at": null, "archived_by": null}, {"id": 11201920194, "node_id": "LA_kwDOAgUK288AAAACm6-8wg", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/labels/backport-to-v3-3-test", "name": "backport-to-v3-3-test", "color": "0e8a16", "default": false, "description": "Backport to v3-3-test", "archived_at": null, "archived_by": null}], "state": "open", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 0, "created_at": "2026-09-27T12:22:58Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T12:23:01Z", "closed_at": null, "assignee": null, "author_association": "MEMBER", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/73787", "html_url": "https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73787", "diff_url": "https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73787.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73787.patch", "merged_at": null}, "body": "Several example Dags built their shell command text from values that are only known at run time \u2014 another task's output, or a Dag param rendered through Jinja. Users copy example Dags into real deployments, so the pattern they show is the pattern that ships. These examples now keep the command text constant and pass the value to the command through `env`, so the shell never parses it as part of the command.\n\nChanged examples:\n\n- `example_dag_decorator` \u2014 the IP address fetched by `get_ip` reaches `echo_ip_info` through `EXTERNAL_IP`.\n- `example_bash_operator` / `example_bash_decorator` \u2014 `show_dag_folder_stats` reads `describe_dag_folder`'s XComs through `env`.\n- edge3 `integration_test` \u2014 `classic_bash` reads `params.mapping_count` through `env`.\n\nA new `check-example-dag-shell-commands` prek hook keeps it that way. On files under `example_dags/` it flags a `bash_command` (or a `@task.bash` return value) built with an f-string, `str.format`, `%` or `+` from a runtime value, and a Jinja expression that renders `xcom_pull`, `params` or `dag_run.conf` into command text. Literals, module-level constants and context values such as `{{ ds }}` are fine. The hook has unit tests under `scripts/tests/ci/prek/`.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n", "closed_by": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/73787/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/73787/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null}
{"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/73786", "repository_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/73786/labels{/name}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/73786/comments", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/73786/events", "html_url": "https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73786", "id": 5602584072, "node_id": "PR_kwDOAgUK288AAAABFWM2kA", "number": 73786, "title": "Keep README stable Airflow version pins in sync with releases", "user": {"login": "potiuk", "id": 595491, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjU5NTQ5MQ==", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/595491?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/potiuk", "html_url": "https://github.com/potiuk", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/potiuk/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/potiuk/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/potiuk/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/potiuk/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/potiuk/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/potiuk/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/potiuk/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/potiuk/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/potiuk/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "labels": [{"id": 1769003317, "node_id": "MDU6TGFiZWwxNzY5MDAzMzE3", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/labels/area:dev-tools", "name": "area:dev-tools", "color": "ededed", "default": false, "description": "", "archived_at": null, "archived_by": null}, {"id": 11201920194, "node_id": "LA_kwDOAgUK288AAAACm6-8wg", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/labels/backport-to-v3-3-test", "name": "backport-to-v3-3-test", "color": "0e8a16", "default": false, "description": "Backport to v3-3-test", "archived_at": null, "archived_by": null}], "state": "open", "locked": false, "assignees": [], "milestone": null, "comments": 0, "created_at": "2026-09-27T12:21:38Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T12:36:45Z", "closed_at": null, "assignee": null, "author_association": "MEMBER", "issue_field_values": [], "type": null, "active_lock_reason": null, "draft": false, "pull_request": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/pulls/73786", "html_url": "https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73786", "diff_url": "https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73786.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/apache/airflow/pull/73786.patch", "merged_at": null}, "body": "The 3.3.2 release (#73279) updated `scripts/ci/prek/supported_versions.py`, which regenerated the version life-cycle table, but the README \"Stable version\" header of the Requirements table and the `pip install` / constraints examples stayed on 3.3.0. Updating those was a separate manual step in the release process, and it was missed (fixed by hand in #73770).\n\nThe `update-supported-versions` hook now takes the stable version from the first row of `SUPPORTED_VERSIONS` and rewrites those pins too, so the release step that edits `supported_versions.py` is enough. The hook fails if any pin site stops matching, so rewording the README cannot silently turn the sync off. The release guide no longer lists the manual step.\n\nThe README / PyPI README changes in this PR are the same as in #73770 and will drop out on rebase once that merges.\n\nrelated: #73770\n\n---\n\n##### Was generative AI tooling used to co-author this PR?\n\n- [X] Yes \u2014 Claude Code (Opus 5)\n\nGenerated-by: Claude Code (Opus 5) following [the guidelines](https://github.com/apache/airflow/blob/main/contributing-docs/05_pull_requests.rst#gen-ai-assisted-contributions)\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n", "closed_by": null, "reactions": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/73786/reactions", "total_count": 0, "+1": 0, "-1": 0, "laugh": 0, "hooray": 0, "confused": 0, "heart": 0, "rocket": 0, "eyes": 0}, "timeline_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/airflow/issues/73786/timeline", "performed_via_github_app": null, "state_reason": null}